t bigger  we're told that they use twice as many  munitions this time and it was focused  very specifically on the chemical  infrastructure but I think some of us  were surprised to find still existed but  weapons research facilities storage  facilities very specifically focused on  that infrastructure you know that last  attack last year 59 Tomahawk missiles  placed on to one airbase there 24 hours  later their airbase was up and running  what do you think the Russian response  will be to this well that is the big  question and and all the briefings last  night we're very careful to point out  that this was not about engaging the  Russians that measures were taken to  avoid Russian casualties but I think the  only answer to that is we will see if  this crosses their red lines and whether  they respond whether in Syria and in  kind or in some other asymmetric kind of  way all of them thank you so much for  joining us Doug pleasure arena
 

